Common Troubleshooting Scenarios for DevOps Engineers

👉 Did you know that most DevOps interviews don’t just test your knowledge of tools (AWS, Jenkins, Docker, Kubernetes)…
They test how you troubleshoot real-world issues under pressure.

Here are some of the most common troubleshooting scenarios I’ve seen (and been asked in interviews):
1️⃣ CI/CD Pipeline Failures
 📌 Scenario: Jenkins/GitHub Actions pipeline fails after code push.
 ⚡ Causes → Incorrect build config, missing env variables, permission errors
 🛠 Fix → Check build logs, validate secrets, re-run with debug enabled

2️⃣ Application Not Accessible After Deployment (502 Bad Gateway)
 📌 Scenario: App deployed on EC2/K8s pod, but URL fails.
 ⚡ Causes → Nginx/Apache misconfig, wrong port binding, container crash
 🛠 Fix → Check logs (docker logs / kubectl logs), verify port mapping, restart service

3️⃣ High Latency / Slow Response
 📌 Scenario: App is up, but users report slowness.
 ⚡ Causes → Auto-scaling misconfigured, DB bottleneck, high CPU usage
 🛠 Fix → Check CloudWatch/Prometheus, optimize queries, enable caching

4️⃣ “ImagePullBackOff” in Kubernetes
 📌 Scenario: Pod stuck in ImagePullBackOff.
 ⚡ Causes → Wrong image tag, missing registry credentials, DNS issues
 🛠 Fix → kubectl describe pod, validate image, add registry secret if needed

5️⃣ Disk Space Issues on Linux Servers
 📌 Scenario: Server stops responding, deployments fail.
 ⚡ Causes → Log files, temp files, large Docker images
 🛠 Fix → df -h, clear /var/log/, docker system prune

6️⃣ AWS IAM Permission Denied
 📌 Scenario: Deployment fails with AccessDenied.
 ⚡ Causes → Wrong IAM policy/role, missing trust relationship
 🛠 Fix → Review IAM JSON, attach correct role, apply least privilege

7️⃣ SSL/TLS Certificate Expired
 📌 Scenario: HTTPS suddenly breaks.
 ⚡ Causes → Missed certificate rotation
 🛠 Fix → Automate renewal with Let’s Encrypt/ACM, set expiry alerts

8️⃣ Terraform State Lock Issues
 📌 Scenario: terraform apply blocked by lock.
 ⚡ Causes → Previous run not released
 🛠 Fix → terraform force-unlock <ID>, use remote state (S3 + DynamoDB)

9️⃣ Docker Container Crashes Immediately
 📌 Scenario: Container exits with code 1.
 ⚡ Causes → Wrong entrypoint, missing dependency, invalid config
 🛠 Fix → Run interactively, check logs, fix Dockerfile

🔟 Load Balancer Health Check Failures
 📌 Scenario: ALB/ELB shows instances as unhealthy.
 ⚡ Causes → Wrong health check path, SG blocking traffic
 🛠 Fix → Verify endpoint, fix SG/NACL, confirm correct port
